WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.180
Speaker 1: We have new swing state polling.&nbsp;
And I want to be really clear about this. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:12.960
is general election swing state polling, which&nbsp;
finds that Ron DeSantis would do better against&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:20.220
Joe Biden than would Donald Trump. This does not&nbsp;
mean the Republican maggots are going to choose&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:25.200
someone other than Trump to be their nominee.&nbsp;
This doesn't mean any of that. Trump is still&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:30.000
the most likely Republican nominee. It just means&nbsp;
that Trump's claim that he would beat Biden where&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:34.740
DeSantis would lose is not borne out by the facts.&nbsp;
Why do we care about swing states? We care about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.740 --> 00:00:39.480
swing states because whether it's the Santos or&nbsp;
Trump, Joe Biden, Biden's going to win California,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:47.640
whether it's the Santos or Trump. DeSantis or&nbsp;
Trump are going to win Wyoming. The election is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:54.180
going to come down to a group of swing states in&nbsp;
those swing states. We are increasingly getting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.180 --> 00:00:59.400
data that Ron DeSantis would do better against&nbsp;
Joe Biden than would Donald Trump. I'm not giving&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:03.300
advice to Republicans. I'm just telling you&nbsp;
this is what the data shows. If you look at a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:10.560
new poll out of Pennsylvania, you find that Biden&nbsp;
leads Trump, but DeSantis leads Biden. Remember,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:14.400
these are hypothetical matchups where you&nbsp;
say to people, if it were Trump versus Biden,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:19.980
who do you vote for? If it were Desanctis versus&nbsp;
Biden, who do you vote for? And people respond.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:27.960
In Georgia, an important state that Joe Biden&nbsp;
won in 2020. Unusually so for Democrats in recent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.960 --> 00:01:35.940
years. In Georgia, Biden leads Trump,&nbsp;
But DeSantis leads Biden. In Arizona,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.940 --> 00:01:43.920
another really important state. Biden leads&nbsp;
Trump. But this. Santos leads Biden. Let's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:49.440
see what else we have from swing states. That may&nbsp;
be it for recent ones. Oh, Michigan. In Michigan,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:55.140
Biden and Trump are tied. DeSantis leads&nbsp;
by a very small margin, statistically,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.140 --> 00:02:02.520
probably a dead heat. So the important takeaway&nbsp;
here is that the Republican electorate right now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:07.860
it's June 27th, right? This could change. Trump&nbsp;
gets arrested a third or fourth time. DeSantis&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.860 --> 00:02:11.880
comes up with some free pony plan that everybody&nbsp;
loves. All of a sudden are free zebras. Who knows?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.880 --> 00:02:18.180
It could change. The point right now is in these&nbsp;
very important contested states, swing states,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.960 --> 00:02:25.740
DeSantis is polling better than Trump against&nbsp;
the most likely Democratic nominee, Joe Biden.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.280 --> 00:02:31.740
So it might be the logical thing for Republicans&nbsp;
to select someone with a better shot at winning,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.740 --> 00:02:34.440
but they seem determined to select Donald Trump.

